Found by reading (bug hunt 2026-09-26); event names are documentation-derived -> langertha-llm-advisor to confirm against lmstudio.ai/docs/developer/rest (streaming events), no live call made.

lib/Langertha/Engine/LMStudio.pm:297 _extract_reasoning_text lifts output[type=reasoning] into Response.thinking on the non-streamed path, but parse_stream_chunk (:509 onward) only handles error, message.delta and chat.end and returns undef for everything else. LM Studio native /api/v1/chat streams reasoning as reasoning.start / reasoning.delta / reasoning.end events, so a streamed call loses the thinking text that the same call returns unstreamed (stream/non-stream divergence, same class as k129 for Ollama/Gemini).

Fix: map reasoning.delta to a Stream::Chunk with thinking => $data->{content} (content ""), so aggregate_thinking rebuilds it; add a parse_stream_chunk test beside t/24_lmstudio_native_input.t, ideally from a captured SSE stream.
